100&amp;w=2048 2048w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/JAY_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=2400 2400w\"/></div><div class=\"_1wu3rm5 _1bw37380\">Jay Peters</div><p class=\"fv263x1\">Posts from this author will be added to your daily email digest and your homepage feed.</p><p class=\"fv263x4\"><a class=\"fv263x5\" href=\"/authors/jay-peters\">See All by <!-- -->Jay Peters</a></p></div></aside> <span class=\"duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup _4aoxp37\">is a senior reporter covering technology, gaming, and more. He joined The Verge in 2019 after nearly two years at Techmeme.</span></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"_1044qiz13\" id=\"zephr-anchor\"><div class=\"duet--article--article-body-component\"><p class=\"duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph _1044qizi _18mzr4b1 _18mzr4b0 _19wv7tc1\">LinkedIn actually announced a \u201cSeems like AI slop\u201d button on July 30th, and the company says that a lot of people have already used it. According to a Thursday post from <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7495960472341409792/\">chief product officer Hari Srinivasan</a>, \u201cover a million people\u201d have clicked on the button, which is accessible from the three dots menu on a post.</p></div><div class=\"duet--article--article-body-component\"><p class=\"duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph _1044qizi _18mzr4b1 _18mzr4b0 _19wv7tc1\">LinkedIn announced the button a few weeks after AI detector Pangram <a href=\"https://www.pangram.com/blog/ai-in-your-feed?ref=404media.co\">determined that</a> 41 percent of LinkedIn\u2019s longform posts were flagged as fully AI generated, <a href=\"https://www.404media.co/linkedin-and-x-are-flooded-with-ai-spam-browsing-data-suggests/\">which <em>404 Media</em> reported on</a>. Alongside the AI slop button, LinkedIn introduced \u201cnew and improved\u201d classifiers to identify posts as AI and removed a feature that would \u201cenhance your post\u201d with AI.</p></div><div class=\"duet--article--article-body-component\"><p class=\"duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph _1044qizi _18mzr4b1 _18mzr4b0 _19wv7tc1\">\u201cAI slop is a top priority for all of us,\u201d Srinivasan said at the time, and it sounds as if the platform\u2019s changes may be making a difference. In Thursday\u2019s post, Srinivasan said that users are overall \u201cnow experiencing 40% less views on what we classify as AI slop from just a few weeks ago.\u201d</p></div><div class=\"duet--article--article-body-component\"><p class=\"duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph _1044qizi _18mzr4b1 _18mzr4b0 _19wv7tc1\">LinkedIn is also adding a new message that will tell users who make a post if \u201cSome members told us this post seems like AI.\u201d</p></div><div class=\"duet--article--article-body-component\"><p class=\"duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph _1044qizi _18mzr4b1 _18mzr4b0 _19wv7tc1\">\u201cWe approached this assuming good intent; I know I\u2019m increasingly conscious on how to not sound like AI &amp; the goal is to provide helpful feedback,\u201d Srinivasan said.</p><img alt=\"A screenshot from LinkedIn showing a message that says: \u201cSome members told us this post seems like Al. We\u2019re sharing this as feedback for you to consider for future posts.\u201d\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=1440\"/></div><div class=\"duet--article--block-placement _1xorkac1 _1xorkac0 duet--article--article-body-component\"><div><div class=\"_1044qizj\"><div class=\"\"><div class=\"duet--media--content-warning _1k8kvzd0\"><div class=\"duet--article--image-gallery-image _1pegheu0\" id=\"dmcyOmltYWdlOjk4MzUwNA==\"><a class=\"_1pegheu1\" data-pswp-height=\"693\" data-pswp-width=\"800\" href=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0,0,100,100\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"A screenshot from LinkedIn showing a message that says: \u201cSome members told us this post seems like Al. We\u2019re sharing this as feedback for you to consider for future posts.\u201d\" class=\"i7ks070\" data-chromatic=\"ignore\" data-nimg=\"fill\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=2400\" srcset=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=256 256w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=376 376w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=384 384w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=415 415w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=480 480w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=540 540w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=640 640w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=750 750w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=828 828w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=1080 1080w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=1200 1200w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=1440 1440w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=1920 1920w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=2048 2048w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/08/1787176243087.jpeg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=2400 2400w\"/></a></div></div></div><div class=\"duet--media--caption _77sxmb0\"><cite class=\"duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup _19wv7tc2 _77sxmb5\">Image: LinkedIn</cite></div></div></div></div><div class=\"duet--article--article-body-component\"><p class=\"duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph _1044qizi _18mzr4b1 _18mzr4b0 _19wv7tc1\">Earlier this year, LinkedIn also said it would be <a href=\"/tech/931667/linkedin-is-cracking-down-on-spammy-ai-generated-comments\">cracking down</a> on comments users create at scale \u201cwith little or no human involvement.\u201d</p></div><div class=\"tly2fw0\"><span class=\"tly2fw2\"><strong>Follow topics and authors</strong> from this story to see more like this in your personalized homepage feed and to receive email updates.</span><ul class=\"tly2fw3\"><li id=\"follow-author-article_footer-dmcyOmF1dGhvclByb2ZpbGU6MTIz\"><span aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-haspopup=\"true\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><span class=\"gnx4pm0 _1uf8q814 _